# set the neighbor type
# skin 65 A instead of r_ribo (100 A). The skin only pads the lists (a pair enters within cutoff + skin; lists are rebuilt
# when an atom has moved half the skin, checked every step after 5). With 100 A a DNA atom's list reached 202 A for the 102 A
# DNA-DNA soft cutoff (PairSoftKokkos 114 us per BD step). 40 A (036) cut the pair time 1.2 s but needed 488 builds instead of 37;
# 65 A is the fitted optimum. "Dangerous builds" in the LAMMPS log must stay 0.
# displacement check every 5 steps (was every step after a delay of 5). Each check is a Kokkos kernel plus a flag copy to
# the host and a sync (~20 us per BD step); with skin 65 A a rebuild is due only every ~190 steps (half-skin 32.5 A), so checking
# every 5 steps keeps a wide margin. LAMMPS still reports "Dangerous builds" (must stay 0).
neighbor 65.0 bin
neigh_modify every 5 delay 5 check yes page 100000 exclude type 1 1

